<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="2b5408ce">&lt;table title=&quot;&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;8&quot; width=&quot;85%&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../core.default.nav_view.base/guidances/concepts/resources/role32.png&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;strong&gt;Roles&lt;/strong&gt; represent a set of skills, competencies, and responsibilities. Roles are not the
                same as rank but describe the characteristics necessary to perform a task or work product responsibilities.
                Roles may represent an individual or a team and a single role may be fulfilled by one or more individuals,
                just as a single individual may perform multiple roles.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../core.default.nav_view.base/guidances/concepts/resources/team32.png&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;strong&gt;Teams&lt;/strong&gt; define a group or organizational unit that is responsible for the completion of a
                set of work. Teams are intended to show how work is allocated across organization with the primary team
                assigned to a task being&amp;nbsp;driven by the primary performer role.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../core.default.nav_view.base/guidances/concepts/resources/workstream32.png&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;strong&gt;Workstreams&lt;/strong&gt; provide views of the published method broken out by individual focus areas
                that depict how the work on the project would typically be divided between different groups or
                sub-projects.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</attribute>
